## What to deliver

Build and rig the Core up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png` matches the
brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together correctly, and the
rig is complete: a broad stepped brass keep of receding tiers rising to a crowned summit,
banners hanging from the upper tiers, a beacon at the very top, and a verdigris accent on
the crown ring and the banner trim sculpted **only** in `#2f7d72` and appearing nowhere
else on the model. **Author the two required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim`
animation subcommands: an **`idle`** (a self-playing loop that turns the beacon and stirs
the banners while the keep stays fixed) and an **`upgrade`** (a one-shot that grinds the
tiers and crown up, flares the beacon, and holds its taller final pose without looping).
The animations and the accent region are the fixed contract — produce all of them; the
parts and joints that realize them are yours. You may add your own extra parts, joints, or
animations on top, but do not drop or contradict the required `idle` and `upgrade`. Before
you finish, run `voxel-anim render` so it emits the per-part `.glb` geometry your result is
built from — an unrendered part is scored as empty (`voxel-anim render --component <part>`
redraws one part; `voxel-anim render --time <ms> --animation <name>` renders the model
posed at that instant of an animation to check the motion). When you are satisfied, stop:
the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
